# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Local development — copy to `.env.local`. The defaults below work as-is with
# `mise run setup` (docker Postgres + local email/password auth). No external
# services (Supabase, Google, Vercel) are required to run locally.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Database — plain Postgres (Drizzle + postgres-js). The default points at the
# docker-compose Postgres started by `mise run db:up`. In production, point this
# at any Postgres server (university host, managed Postgres, ...).
#
# If host port 5432 is already taken (e.g. another local Postgres), put
# `DB_PORT=5433` in a local `.env` file (docker compose reads it) and change the
# `:5432` below to match.
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://saude:saude@localhost:5432/saude_territorial

# Better Auth — required. The value below is a throwaway dev secret; generate a
# real one for any shared/hosted environment (`openssl rand -base64 32`).
BETTER_AUTH_SECRET=dev-secret-change-me-in-production
BETTER_AUTH_URL=http://localhost:3000

# App
NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL=http://localhost:3000

# ── Optional ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Google OAuth (identity only — no Sheets/Drive scopes). OPTIONAL: leave unset
# to run with email/password only. When both are set, a "Entrar com Google"
# button appears on the login page alongside the email/password form.
# GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
# GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=

# OSRM (routing) — defaults to the public demo server. Set to a self-hosted OSRM
# base URL for production. See src/lib/routing/client.ts.
# OSRM_BASE_URL=https://router.project-osrm.org
